{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GraphGeneration","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every structural mutation (an insertion, a removal, re-pointing an edge) starts a new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generation. Reserving capacity and writing attached map values do not. A structure derived from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a graph stores the graph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"generation"},{"type":"text","text":" and calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCurrent(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" before it relies on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A copy of a graph has the same generation as the original until either is mutated. Views and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"adaptors (a transposed view, an undirected view, a wrapper such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report their base’s generation, so a view and its base, though they may describe different"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graphs, have equal generations. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCurrent(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" answers only whether the storage of the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passed in is in the state the generation was read from; it does not tell which view the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generation was read through. An untracked generation, from a representation that does not track"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generations or a mutable graph never mutated, is current for no graph. Equal tracked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generations are the same structural state of the same storage, and every untracked generation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equals every other."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A10GenerationV","role":"symbol","title":"GraphGeneration","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GraphGeneration"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GraphGeneration"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration.swift#L57","fileName":"GraphGeneration.swift"}},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A graph’s generation: which structural state of which graph storage it is."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-1rsfw","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-1t817","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-3zt2o","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-5kltt","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-scjl"]},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphPro